Sets what an action animates TO. The patch is the action's end state and MERGES into it key by key at every depth (a one-key shadow keeps the rest of it); a key set to null is REMOVED from the end state, so that property stops being animated. Groups are video, audio and text, with the same keys as set_video / set_audio / set_text — a colour is FOUR numbers here too, and it ramps in OKLab with straight alpha, as a graphic colour does; video.chroma.key's three numbers do too. A bad key or value is refused by its path with the group in it (video.filters[1].kind), though values are NOT range-checked: an animation may aim past what a stored property could hold. These keys are refused: video.motion, a preset anchored to the clip's two ends rather than a value to ramp between (set it with set_video), text.words, whose times belong to speech, and video.cutout.subject and video.cutout.quality, the clip's own (set them with set_video; a cutout's edge, feather and background animate). In audio, every key the sound's effects read animates — pan, mono, channels, eq, hum, noise_reduction, gate, leveller, de_esser, compressor, limiter and isolation, beside volume and the fades: numbers ramp, and a switch (a group or an EQ slot turned on, mono, channels, an EQ slope, hum's frequency and harmonics, the leveller's response) changes when the action ENDS; isolation ramps from 0 on a clip with none. duck, keep_pitch, the fade shapes and voice are stored but never animate. A GRAPHIC clip's props are a fourth group, graphic: {props: {<key>: <value>}}, keyed by its module's schema and checked as set_graphic checks them, min and max included, against the module as graphics/ holds it NOW; the app reads that schema, so never send one. A number and a colour ramp along the curve: a number arrives with decimals (64 to 129 is 96.5 halfway), so a module that needs a whole number rounds it, and a colour blends in OKLab, as interpolateColors does, with straight alpha. A string, a boolean and an enum switch to the end's value when the action ENDS. An image (asset) prop switches to the end's image when the action ENDS; "" names no image there (null removes the prop from the end). A prop its module marks animate: false is refused: set it with set_graphic. A prop the clip holds no value for starts from the module's current default, written into the clip in the same undo step. graphic.props.<key>: null removes that prop from the end, graphic: null the whole group. get_project shows kinds beside props; the app writes it and ignores one you send, so an end read back can be sent again. While the module is missing or does not compile a prop value is refused (needs its module's schema) — get_graphic says why — and a null still removes. speed, a number beside the groups, is a MEDIA clip's rate (×0.1–×1000, clamped): the clip ramps from the rate in force to it along the curve and holds it after; the clip keeps its start and length and plays more or less source, and an end rate that would read past the end of its media is refused, naming the largest end rate that fits. speed: null removes it. Above ×12 the clip's audio is left out, and the answer carries audio_left_out and audio_note. With speed in the patch, captions on a Captions track wholly inside a clip with sound are re-timed with it in the same step: captions_retimed lists them, and captions_removed those whose speech it no longer plays.
